<%# Crawl fallback for pages whose text exists only inside the Inertia payload: a fetcher
    that does not run JavaScript otherwise receives an empty shell. noscript keeps it out
    of the rendered UI, where the React component already shows the same article.
    The bodies are already escaped or repo-authored; the gsub is the one guarantee that
    matters here, since a literal closing tag would end the raw-text element early. %>
<noscript>
  <article>
    <h1><%= @seo_article_fallback[:title] %></h1>
    <%= @seo_article_fallback[:html].to_s.gsub(%r{</noscript}i, "&lt;/noscript").html_safe %>
  </article>
</noscript>
